## Conclusion
In summary, a series of donor-acceptor heterostructure crystals have been obtained by using host-guest structures as a platform. These heterostructure crystals exhibit spatially segregated multicolor emission performance resulting from different CT transition between various donors (guests) and the tpt acceptor (host). Furthermore, we successfully controlled the morphology of the resulting crystals and investigated the energy transfer process between adjacent domains in heterostructure crystals. Moreover, an optical logic gate prototype was isolated and tested based on the heterostructure crystals, thus indicating the potential for heterocrystals to be used in integrated photonic logic circuitry. The results reported herein may provide a new perspective for the rational construction of heterocompositional and multifunctional crystalline materials. The development of a novel facile synthetic methodology for the preparation of donor-acceptor heterostructure crystals based on the further exploration of donor-acceptor interactions is ongoing in our group.
